# /etc/apt/preferences.d/pinning - archive pinning for the fleet snapshot.
# The release process treats a version as installable when at least one of
# these stanzas matches it; docs/policy.md spells the rules out in prose.

Explanation: the Debian archive (signed by the Debian archive signing key)
Package: *
Pin: release o=Debian
Pin-Priority: 700

Explanation: anything shipping the bookworm codename, whatever the archive
Package: *
Pin: release a=bookworm
Pin-Priority: 650

Explanation: the main component of any archive
Package: *
Pin: release c=main
Pin-Priority: 600

Explanation: the vetted 5.0.* tool series
Package: *
Pin: version 5.0.*
Pin-Priority: 900
